## 1. Project Understanding

### What problem this project solves

EventHub is a **full-stack event booking platform** that enables users to discover events, view real-time seat availability, and reserve seats through an atomic, race-condition-safe booking mechanism. It solves the dual problem of (a) providing a polished event discovery experience and (b) ensuring seat inventory integrity under concurrent load — preventing the classic "two users book the last seat" overselling bug.

### Target users

| User Segment | Description |
|---|---|
| **Event attendees** | General public who want to browse, discover, and book seats for events (concerts, conferences, workshops, etc.) |
| **System administrators** | (Future scope) Event organizers who create and manage their events |

### Primary goals

1. Demonstrate full-stack engineering capability: React frontend, Node/Express API, MongoDB persistence
2. Implement secure JWT-based authentication (register, login, logout)
3. Build a browseable, searchable, paginated event catalog
4. Execute atomic seat booking that is concurrency-safe (no overselling)
5. Provide real-time seat availability updates via WebSockets
6. Offer AI-powered natural language event search

### Expected outcome

A deployed, production-ready web application that a hiring reviewer can interact with — registering an account, browsing events, booking seats, observing real-time seat updates across browser tabs, and cancelling bookings — all with a premium dark-themed UI.

### Core value proposition

**Atomic concurrency-safe booking + real-time seat updates + AI-powered search** — three advanced features that elevate this beyond a typical CRUD demo into a system that demonstrates production-level architectural thinking.

