## 4. Complete Website Flow

### Primary Happy Path

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Landing / Home Page] --> B{User logged in?}
    B -->|No| C[Browse Events as Guest]
    B -->|Yes| D[Browse Events with Auth]
    
    C --> E[Click Event Card]
    D --> E
    
    E --> F[Event Detail Page]
    F --> G{Click Book Seats}
    
    G -->|Not Logged In| H[Redirect to Login]
    G -->|Logged In| I[Booking Form + Modal]
    
    H --> J[Login Page]
    J -->|Success| K[Redirect back to Event]
    J -->|Has no account| L[Register Page]
    L -->|Success| K
    
    I --> M{Confirm Booking?}
    M -->|Cancel| F
    M -->|Confirm| N[POST /api/bookings]
    
    N -->|201 Success| O[Toast: Booked! + Seat Update]
    N -->|409 Conflict| P[Toast: Not enough seats]
    N -->|400 Bad Request| Q[Toast: Validation error]
    
    O --> R[My Bookings Page]
    R --> S{Cancel Booking?}
    S -->|Yes| T[DELETE /api/bookings/:id]
    T --> U[Toast: Cancelled + Seats Released]
```

### Alternate Flows

#### Guest Attempting to Book
1. Guest clicks "Book Now" on Event Detail Page
2. `ProtectedRoute` intercepts → Redirect to `/login`
3. User logs in or registers
4. Redirect back to Home (or ideally the original event page)

#### Invalid Login
1. User enters wrong email/password on Login Page
2. Server returns 401
3. Toast: "Invalid email or password"
4. User stays on Login Page, form is not cleared

#### Token Expiration
1. User is logged in, token expires
2. Any API call returns 401
3. Axios response interceptor catches it
4. Auth store cleared, user redirected to `/login`
5. Toast would inform user (implicit via page redirect)

#### Booking Race Condition (Concurrent Users)
1. Two users view the same event with 1 seat left
2. Both click "Book 1 seat" simultaneously
3. First request: `findOneAndUpdate` succeeds → seat decremented to 0 → booking created
4. Second request: `findOneAndUpdate` returns `null` (availableSeats 0 < 1) → 409 returned
5. Both users receive Socket.IO `seatUpdate` showing 0 seats
6. Exactly one booking is created — zero overselling

#### Returning User
1. User visits site → Zustand `persist` middleware loads token from localStorage
2. If token is valid, user sees authenticated navbar (name + logout button)
3. If token expired, first API call triggers 401 → auto-logout

