## 5. Navigation Structure

### Navbar (All Pages)

| Element | Purpose | Visibility |
|---|---|---|
| **Logo "EventHub"** | Brand identity + link to Home | Always |
| **My Bookings** link | Navigate to bookings page | Authenticated only |
| **User Avatar + Name** | Identity indicator | Authenticated only |
| **Logout** button | Clear auth state | Authenticated only |
| **Login** button | Navigate to login | Unauthenticated only |
| **Register** button | Navigate to registration | Unauthenticated only |

**Why**: Single persistent navbar provides consistent navigation across all pages. Conditional rendering based on auth state guides users to appropriate actions.

### Footer (All Pages)

| Element | Purpose |
|---|---|
| **Copyright text** | Legal requirement |
| **"Built with React & Node.js"** | Tech attribution |

**Why**: Minimal footer keeps focus on content. Does not distract from the primary event-browsing experience.

### Mobile Navigation

- Hamburger menu icon on small screens
- Mobile menu slides out with the same links
- Auto-closes on navigation

**Why**: Standard responsive pattern. Category filters on Home Page scroll horizontally with `overflow-x-auto` for touch.

### No Sidebar

**Why**: The application is a linear browsing experience (list → detail → book), not a dashboard with multiple parallel features. A sidebar would add unnecessary navigation complexity.

