## 11. Data Flow Diagram

### Flow 1: User Registration

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant U as User (Browser)
    participant R as React (RegisterPage)
    participant A as Axios Client
    participant S as Express Server
    participant V as Zod Validator
    participant AS as Auth Service
    participant DB as MongoDB

    U->>R: Fill name, email, password
    R->>A: POST /api/auth/register
    A->>S: HTTP Request
    S->>V: validate(registerSchema)
    V-->>S: ✅ Parsed body
    S->>AS: register({ name, email, password })
    AS->>DB: User.findOne({ email })
    DB-->>AS: null (no duplicate)
    AS->>AS: bcrypt.hash(password, 12)
    AS->>DB: User.create({ name, email, passwordHash })
    DB-->>AS: User document
    AS->>AS: jwt.sign({ userId })
    AS-->>S: { token, user }
    S-->>A: 201 { success, data: { token, user } }
    A-->>R: Response
    R->>R: authStore.setAuth(user, token)
    R->>R: navigate('/')
    R->>U: Toast: "Account created!"
```

### Flow 2: Atomic Seat Booking (Critical Path)

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant U as User
    participant R as React (BookingForm)
    participant A as Axios
    participant S as Express
    participant Auth as Auth Middleware
    participant V as Zod
    participant BS as Booking Service
    participant DB as MongoDB
    participant IO as Socket.IO

    U->>R: Click "Book 3 seats"
    R->>R: Show confirmation Modal
    U->>R: Click "Confirm"
    R->>A: POST /api/bookings { eventId, seats: 3 }
    A->>S: HTTP + Bearer token
    S->>Auth: authenticate(JWT)
    Auth-->>S: req.userId set
    S->>V: validate(createBookingSchema)
    V-->>S: ✅ Valid
    S->>BS: createBooking(userId, eventId, 3)
    
    Note over BS,DB: ATOMIC OPERATION
    BS->>DB: Event.findById(eventId)
    DB-->>BS: event (exists, future date ✅)
    BS->>DB: Event.findOneAndUpdate(<br/>{ _id, availableSeats: {$gte: 3} },<br/>{ $inc: {availableSeats: -3} },<br/>{ new: true })
    DB-->>BS: updatedEvent (or null if insufficient)
    
    alt Seats available
        BS->>DB: Booking.create({ user, event, seats, status })
        DB-->>BS: booking
        BS->>IO: emit('seatUpdate', { eventId, availableSeats })
        IO->>IO: Broadcast to room event:{id}
        BS-->>S: booking
        S-->>A: 201 { success, data: booking }
        A-->>R: Success
        R->>U: Toast: "Booked 3 seats!"
    else Not enough seats
        BS-->>S: throw ApiError(409)
        S-->>A: 409 { error: "Not enough seats" }
        A-->>R: Error
        R->>U: Toast: "Not enough seats"
    end
```

### Flow 3: Real-Time Seat Update (Socket.IO)

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant U1 as User A (Books)
    participant U2 as User B (Watching)
    participant Server as Node.js Server
    participant IO as Socket.IO
    participant TQ as TanStack Query (User B)

    Note over U2,IO: User B viewing Event Detail Page
    U2->>IO: emit('joinEvent', eventId)
    IO->>IO: socket.join('event:{id}')
    
    Note over U1,Server: User A books 2 seats
    U1->>Server: POST /api/bookings
    Server->>Server: Atomic decrement
    Server->>IO: emit('seatUpdate') to room
    
    IO->>U2: seatUpdate { eventId, availableSeats: 48 }
    U2->>TQ: queryClient.setQueryData(['event', id], patched)
    TQ->>U2: Re-render SeatCounter instantly
    
    Note over U2: No HTTP refetch. No loading spinner.
```

