## 13. State Management Plan

| State Category | Technology | What's Stored | Why This Choice |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Auth (Global, Persistent)** | Zustand + `persist` | `{ user, token }` | Must survive page refreshes via localStorage. Accessed by Axios interceptor outside React tree via `getState()`. |
| **Server State (Cached)** | TanStack Query | Events list, event detail, user bookings | Automatic caching, background refetch, stale-while-revalidate, deduplication. Eliminates manual loading/error state management. |
| **Real-Time State** | Socket.IO → TanStack Query cache patch | Live seat counts | Socket events directly patch TanStack Query cache via `queryClient.setQueryData()`. No separate real-time store needed. |
| **Form State (Local)** | React `useState` | Login form, register form, booking form, search input | Form state is local to the component lifecycle. No need for global persistence. |
| **UI State (Local)** | React `useState` | Modal open/close, password visibility toggle, mobile menu open | Ephemeral UI state. Doesn't need to survive unmount. |
| **Pagination (Local)** | React `useState` + query params | Current page, active category filter | Resets on navigation. Could be promoted to URL params for shareability. |

### Why NOT Redux

Zustand + TanStack Query provides equivalent functionality with dramatically less boilerplate. Zustand handles the tiny amount of global state (auth), while TanStack Query handles all server state with built-in loading/error/caching. Redux would be over-engineering for this scope.

