## 16. Authentication & Authorization Flow

### Login Process

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant C as Client
    participant S as Server
    participant DB as MongoDB

    C->>S: POST /api/auth/login { email, password }
    S->>S: Zod validate body
    S->>DB: User.findOne({ email }).select('+passwordHash')
    DB-->>S: user (or null)
    
    alt User not found
        S-->>C: 401 "Invalid email or password"
    else User found
        S->>S: bcrypt.compare(password, user.passwordHash)
        alt Password mismatch
            S-->>C: 401 "Invalid email or password"
        else Password matches
            S->>S: jwt.sign({ userId }, JWT_SECRET, { expiresIn: '7d' })
            S-->>C: 200 { token, user: { id, name, email } }
        end
    end
    
    C->>C: zustand.setAuth(user, token)
    C->>C: localStorage persists via zustand/persist
```

### Session Handling

- **Stateless**: No server-side sessions. JWT contains `userId` + expiry.
- **Storage**: Token stored in Zustand → persisted to `localStorage` under key `event-booking-auth`.
- **Attachment**: Axios request interceptor reads `useAuthStore.getState().token` and sets `Authorization: Bearer {token}` header.

### Token Lifecycle

| Event | Action |
|---|---|
| Login/Register | New JWT issued (7-day expiry) |
| Every API request | Token attached via Axios interceptor |
| Token valid | Server extracts `userId` from payload |
| Token expired | Server returns 401; client interceptor calls `logout()` and redirects to `/login` |
| User clicks Logout | Client calls `authStore.logout()` → clears token + user from store + localStorage |

### Permission Checking

```
Request → auth.middleware.js → check Authorization header
                             → jwt.verify(token, secret)
                             → attach req.userId
                             → next()

For booking cancellation:
Request → authenticate → ownership.js → Booking.findById(id)
                                       → compare booking.user vs req.userId
                                       → 403 if mismatch
                                       → next()
```

### Protected Routes (Frontend)

```jsx
<ProtectedRoute>  // Checks useAuthStore().token
  <BookingsPage />  // Only renders if authenticated
</ProtectedRoute>  // Else: redirect to /login
```

