## 19. Performance Strategy

| Strategy | Implementation | Impact |
|---|---|---|
| **Server-side pagination** | Offset-based, 12 events per page, max 50 | Prevents loading thousands of events |
| **Database indexes** | Compound index on `{ category, date, availableSeats }` | Sub-millisecond filtered queries |
| **TanStack Query caching** | `staleTime: 30s` globally, `10s` for event detail | Reduces redundant API calls |
| **Socket.IO cache patching** | Direct `setQueryData()` instead of refetch | Zero-flicker real-time updates |
| **Lazy-evaluated auth** | `useAuthStore.getState()` (no subscription) in Axios interceptor | No unnecessary re-renders |
| **Code splitting** | Vite automatic chunk splitting | Only loads JS for current route |
| **Minimal bundle** | Lucide tree-shakes unused icons. No heavy UI framework. | 411KB JS, 31KB CSS (gzipped: 131KB + 6KB) |
| **WebSocket transport** | Socket.IO prefers WebSocket, falls back to polling | Lowest latency for real-time updates |
| **Atomic operations** | `findOneAndUpdate` instead of read-then-write | Single DB roundtrip per booking |
| **Mongoose `select: false`** | passwordHash never sent over the wire | Reduces payload size + security |

### Future Optimizations

- Route-level code splitting with `React.lazy()` + `Suspense`
- Image optimization (WebP, lazy loading, CDN)
- API response compression (gzip/brotli via Express middleware)
- Redis caching layer for event listings
- Connection pooling tuning for MongoDB

